# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  FAAPS Mobile — runtime configuration (template)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and set the API base
#  URL for YOUR machine. Never commit a LAN IP.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
#  Every variable here is inlined into the JS bundle at build time
#  by the Expo CLI, so never put a secret in an EXPO_PUBLIC_* var.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Base URL of the FAAPS backend.
#
# The trailing `/api` is optional — `src/config/api.ts` normalises the
# value and strips a trailing `/api`, because every service path in
# `src/lib/api/*` already starts with `/api` (e.g. `/api/student/profile`).
# Both of these work and resolve to the same requests:
#
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://<your-lan-ip>:8080/api
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://<your-lan-ip>:8080
#
# Special hosts:
#   • Android emulator  →  http://10.0.2.2:8080
#   • iOS simulator     →  http://localhost:8080
#   • Physical device   →  http://<your-lan-ip>:8080   ← use this one
#
#   Find your LAN IP:
#     Windows      →  ipconfig  (IPv4 Address)
#     macOS/Linux  →  ifconfig | grep 'inet '
#
#   The phone and the computer must be on the SAME Wi-Fi network, and
#   the FAAPS backend must listen on 0.0.0.0:8080 (not just 127.0.0.1)
#   for the phone to reach it.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api
